.TH XUR.STD.PROCESS 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.process \- spawning and controlling child processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::process;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::process
starts OS child processes and waits for them to finish.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B spawn(program, args) -> Result<Process, str>
Start a new process with the given program path and argument list.
.SH PROCESS METHODS
.TP
.B pid() -> i64
The process ID of the child.
.TP
.B kill()
Send a kill signal to the child.
.TP
.B wait() -> Result<i64, str>
Wait for the child to exit and return its exit code.
.TP
.B try_wait() -> Result<Option<i64>, str>
Check whether the child has exited without blocking.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::process;
use std::io;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let child = process::spawn("echo", ["hello"])?;
    let code = child.wait()?;
    io::println("exited with {}", code);
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7)
